WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.133
Tool results are an injection channel.

2
00:00:02.413 --> 00:00:06.595
Lesson 10 treated tool results as data flowing back to the model.

3
00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:10.203
They are also a way for other people’s text to reach your model.

4
00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:14.216
A meeting transcript contains whatever anyone said in the meeting.

5
00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:20.512
A fetched web page, an inbound email, or a ticket description contains whatever its author wrote.

6
00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:28.899
If that text says “ignore your previous instructions and do something else,” the model reads it in the same context as your instructions.

7
00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:36.752
This is indirect prompt injection, and the OWASP Top 10 for LLM applications lists prompt injection first.

8
00:00:37.032 --> 00:00:40.232
Anthropic’s guidance for this threat model has several parts.

9
00:00:40.512 --> 00:00:46.528
Put untrusted content only in tool results, never in the system prompt or plain user text.

10
00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:52.440
Say what the content is and where it came from, in the tool’s description or in the result itself.

11
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:59.483
State the policy in the system prompt: content from tools is data and must never override the user’s request.

12
00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:04.051
JSON-encode untrusted strings so they cannot break out of their delimiters.

13
00:01:04.331 --> 00:01:10.965
Do not put your own instructions inside tool results, since the model is trained to treat those with skepticism.

14
00:01:11.245 --> 00:01:12.269
Limit access.

15
00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:19.397
And optionally, screen tool outputs with a small, inexpensive classifier call before the main model sees them.

16
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:25.459
The docs present these as layers to combine, not as one fix, and none of them comes with a guarantee.

17
00:01:25.739 --> 00:01:40.053
That is why the design controls in this lesson matter more than any prompt: an agent that cannot send email cannot be tricked into sending one, and a write that needs a human’s approval needs that approval even when the model has been fooled.
